body: "## Evidence\nPR #211 at `2a898d448c49ee5ddb3af40820cca3db5f834b70` upgrades SDK2026.10.28 to2026.10.30. Both Node22 and Node26 stop at440/446 passing tests; six native shared-evidence tests fail with `--parent must not use placeholder token \"none\". Use --unset parent to clear this field.`\nhttps://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/41698956515/job/126177496307\nhttps://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/41698956515/job/126177496272\n\nExact fixture evidence: `tracker()` passes parent/goal/objective/assignee:`\"none\"` at shared-evidence.test.ts31. The reference-closure fixture repeats it at shared-reference-closure.test.ts97; additional updates also use sentinels.\nhttps://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/2a898d448c49ee5ddb3af40820cca3db5f834b70/test/shared-evidence.test.ts#L31\nhttps://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/2a898d448c49ee5ddb3af40820cca3db5f834b70/test/shared-reference-closure.test.ts#L97\n\nThe aborted cases cover twenty bindings/one fragment, finite JSON fidelity,500 seeded native-state sequences, competing SDK transitions, installed no-Git CLI behavior, and expanded/factored native references. Aggregate coverage also falls below unchanged gates after these refusals.\n\n## Goal and expected behavior\nThe delivered shared-fragment feature requires complete citation paths, distinct revision identity and equivalent expanded/factored coverage:\nhttps://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/800b5af548ec1e7f765c4a441316c147eca2a8f7/.agents/pm/features/pm-context-shared-fragment-evidence.toon\n\nFixtures must initialize and mutate through the supported SDK clearing contract so these regressions actually reach their behavioral assertions on the upgraded SDK.\n\n## Acceptance and limits\nMigrate all affected fixture create/update/child-process calls to typed clearing semantics while preserving ambient-focus non-inheritance, all500 seeds, history/ABA/revision assertions, no-mutation checks and installed no-Git coverage. Restore full Node22/26 and packed gates at unchanged thresholds. Do not remove real SDK calls or replace them with mocks to make acceptance green.\n\nThis is a bounded fixture/upgrade acceptance defect, not evidence that production shared-evidence reads corrupt or mutate trackers. Exact immutable source and hosted logs were inspected; no local whole-suite rerun. All211 issue/PR bodies and101 current canonical records were checked; no existing owner for this SDK10.30 refusal was found. #197 is the separate resolved ENOTEMPTY cleanup failure.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-04T21:28:32Z)\n>\n> Fixed by #211 (merged as 363e8bc): the six shared-evidence regressions now clear typed fields with `unset` (pm-cli GH-1614), and coverage passes at unchanged thresholds on pm-cli 2026.11.4."
